\ Exact closed-form weave counts when at most two months remain.
\ A suffix can contain only unfinished months, because all other
\ month counts are already zero. Their ordinal identities are kept.
\
\ Zero unfinished months: exactly one empty suffix.
\ One unfinished month: exactly one uniform suffix.
\ Two unfinished months i<j with a remaining days, b remaining days:
\   If i has not started, it must appear FIRST and j must appear LAST:
\     C(a+b-2, a-1).
\   If i has already started, only the final-occurrence restriction
\   remains, so j must appear LAST:
\     C(a+b-1, a).
\ A state with j already started but i never started cannot be reached
\ through any legal weaving; reject it rather than inventing a count.
\
\ This exact shortcut does not add an entry to the memoization cache.
\ It does not replace the general recurrence for three or more months.
\ No nested loop is used. CAL execution remains unverified.

A short weaving suffix has
  a number called completed,
  a number called unfinished,
  a number called first remaining,
  a number called second remaining,
  a number called first started,
  a number called second started,
  a wide quantity called completions.

The short weaving suffix is a short weaving suffix.
The short month state is a woven month state.

\ Typed small binomial operands avoid CAL treating descriptive locals as types.
The shortbinomialtop is a number.
The shortbinomialbottom is a number.

\ Record at most two positive remaining counts in ascending month order.
To inspect unfinished short months:
  Put 0 into the short weaving suffix's unfinished.
  Put 1 into the short weaving suffix's completed.
  Put the woven month states' first into the short month state.
  Loop.
    If the short month state is nil, break.
    If the short month state's remaining days is greater than 0,
      remember the unfinished short month.
    If the short weaving suffix's unfinished is greater than 2,
      put 0 into the short weaving suffix's completed; exit.
    Put the short month state's next into the short month state.
  Repeat.

To remember the unfinished short month:
  Add 1 to the short weaving suffix's unfinished.
  If the short weaving suffix's unfinished is 1,
    remember the first short month; exit.
  If the short weaving suffix's unfinished is 2,
    remember the second short month.

To remember the first short month:
  Put the short month state's remaining days into the short weaving suffix's first remaining.
  Put 0 into the short weaving suffix's first started.
  If the short month state's remaining days is less than the short month state's total days,
    put 1 into the short weaving suffix's first started.

To remember the second short month:
  Put the short month state's remaining days into the short weaving suffix's second remaining.
  Put 0 into the short weaving suffix's second started.
  If the short month state's remaining days is less than the short month state's total days,
    put 1 into the short weaving suffix's second started.

\ If one or no months remain, the only legal continuation repeats
\ the sole remaining month until all its days have been consumed.
To count a short weaving suffix:
  Inspect unfinished short months.
  If the short weaving suffix's completed is 0, exit.
  Put "1" into the short weaving suffix's completions.
  If the short weaving suffix's unfinished is less than 2, exit.
  If the short weaving suffix's first started is 0,
    count unstarted first month completions; exit.
  Put the short weaving suffix's first remaining into the shortbinomialtop.
  Add the short weaving suffix's second remaining to the shortbinomialtop.
  Subtract 1 from the shortbinomialtop.
  Calculate binomial coefficients given the shortbinomialtop and the short weaving suffix's first remaining.
  Put the binomial result into the short weaving suffix's completions.

\ The lower-index month has not started. The higher-index month must
\ also be unstarted, and the first/last letters are forced.
To count unstarted first month completions:
  Put "0" into the short weaving suffix's completions.
  If the short weaving suffix's second started is 1, exit.
  Put the short weaving suffix's first remaining into the shortbinomialtop.
  Add the short weaving suffix's second remaining to the shortbinomialtop.
  Subtract 2 from the shortbinomialtop.
  Put the short weaving suffix's first remaining into the shortbinomialbottom.
  Subtract 1 from the shortbinomialbottom.
  Calculate binomial coefficients given the shortbinomialtop and the shortbinomialbottom.
  Put the binomial result into the short weaving suffix's completions.
